wm2-born-again -- attribution and upstream terms
=================================================

This file records where this program comes from. The licence itself is in
LICENSE, and is the MIT licence.

This software is derived from wm2 by Chris Cannam (cannam@all-day-breakfast.com),
originally released in March 1997. The original wm2 source code is included in
the upstream-wm2/ directory for reference.

The original wm2 carried no formal licence file. The terms Chris Cannam gave in
its README were:

    "If you want to hack the code into something else for your own amusement,
    please go ahead.  Feel free to modify and redistribute, as long as you
    retain the original copyrights as appropriate."

That condition is met by retaining his copyright above, and the MIT licence
imposes the same requirement on this work.

wm2 itself began as a derivative of "9wm" by David Hogan, and used the
"xvertext" font rotation library version 2.0 by Alan Richardson. The sideways
tabs were Andy Green's idea. This version no longer uses xvertext: the rotated
tab label is drawn by Xft with a rotation matrix, so that credit is historical
rather than a dependency of the compiled program.
